{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsaZrFH7XYcvQQR7YEtJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014g1yAgogy9uDouNMfqiKPw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t01/shadow/exec-ws/decision.json","content":"{\n  \"decision\": \"CREATE\",\n  \"reasons\": [\n    \"Q2's admissibility condition (E-B) requires an encode(d) author who has never accessed reference.py nor any analysis derived from it. This session read reference.py at observe-evidence, so no artifact authored in-session can satisfy E-B; only a separately launched, input-restricted process can.\",\n    \"The trial contract K-E6-trial permits creation (may_create_creator: true, may_realize_creation: true, max_children: 1, max_depth: 1) and the selected harness carries a create branch gated by validate-child and the deterministic fresh launcher, so an isolated clean-room child is realizable within governance.\",\n    \"The causal-separation condition of E-B is satisfiable by manifest restriction: the child needs only package/artifacts/format.md and package/artifacts/probes.json, both of which exist verbatim in the package and are not derived from reference.py.\",\n    \"Nothing is lost relative to the local branch: Q1 (E-A) has no authorship constraint and is resolvable in-session from workspace evidence, while Q3 and Q4 are deterministic functions of the child deliverable under a pre-committed integration rule. The CREATE branch therefore dominates: it settles everything the local branch could plus the distinctions the local branch provably cannot.\"\n  ]\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":844,"cache_read_input_tokens":47912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":844},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":